// =====================================================================================
// P6W_SETUP_PATCH_04.dax  -  BUILD 2026-11-12a  -  R collateral buckets labelled in external-rating terms (Will 9 Nov)
// Replaces the calculated table P6W Rating Map. Same Bucket Order numbers (1-6, 9) and the same Low Grade flag, so no
// measure changes; only the legend text. New column [Internal] lists the internal grades in each bucket (tooltips).
// Mapping internal A+/A ≈ AAA-AA · B+/B ≈ A · C+/C/C- ≈ BBB · D+/D ≈ BB · D- and below ≈ B and lower — checked 11 Nov
// against S&P / Moody's on the rated part of HF collateral (P6A_PAPER_RATING_CHECK RC2): A+ = AAA/AA, B+ = AA/A, C+ = BBB.
// CHECK it worked: R1 / R2 legend reads AAA–AA, A, BBB, BB, B & below, No bond detail (not A, B, C, D, D- and below).
// HOW: Data pane ▸ P6W Rating Map ▸ formula bar ▸ Ctrl+A ▸ paste ▸ Enter. Then [Bucket] ▸ Sort by column ▸ Bucket Order;
//      hide Rating_ssj, Bucket Order, Low Grade, Internal. In R1 / R2 re-pick the legend colours (labels changed).
// =====================================================================================

P6W Rating Map =
VAR rm_vals = CALCULATETABLE ( DISTINCT ( FACT_ALLREPO[Rating_ssj] ), REMOVEFILTERS () )
VAR rm_tagged =
    ADDCOLUMNS (
        SELECTCOLUMNS ( rm_vals, "Rating_ssj", FACT_ALLREPO[Rating_ssj] ),
        "@r", UPPER ( TRIM ( [Rating_ssj] ) )
    )
VAR rm_b =
    ADDCOLUMNS (
        rm_tagged,
        "@b",
            SWITCH (
                TRUE (),
                ISBLANK ( [Rating_ssj] ) || [@r] = "" || CONTAINSSTRING ( [@r], "NOT IDENTIFIED" ), 6,
                LEFT ( [@r], 1 ) = "A", 1,
                LEFT ( [@r], 1 ) = "B", 2,
                LEFT ( [@r], 1 ) = "C", 3,
                [@r] IN { "D+", "D" }, 4,
                [@r] = "D-" || LEFT ( [@r], 1 ) IN { "E", "F", "Z" }, 5,
                9
            )
    )
RETURN
    SELECTCOLUMNS (
        rm_b,
        "Rating_ssj", [Rating_ssj],
        "Bucket", SWITCH ( [@b], 1, "AAA–AA", 2, "A", 3, "BBB", 4, "BB", 5, "B & below", 6, "No bond detail", "Unmapped" ),
        "Bucket Order", [@b],
        "Low Grade", IF ( [@b] = 5, 1, 0 ),
        "Internal", SWITCH ( [@b], 1, "A+ A", 2, "B+ B", 3, "C+ C C-", 4, "D+ D", 5, "D- E F Z", 6, "blank / not identified", "other" )
    )







// =====================================================================================
// P6W_SETUP_PATCH_06.dax  -  BUILD 2026-11-11a  -  R1 "Compare" row label follows R1a (1M ago … 2Y ago)
// Run BEFORE P6A_MEASURES_TE2.csx build 11a (the script stops if P6W R Row[Days] is missing).
// How it works: one compare row per R1a window. P6 R1 Collateral returns blank on the rows that do not match the R1a
// pick, and a bar chart hides a category with no value, so R1 always shows 2 bars: "As of" + "<window> ago".
// =====================================================================================

// ---- S1 select the table P6W R Row ▸ replace its formula ▸ Enter

P6W R Row =
DATATABLE (
    "Row", STRING,
    "Order", INTEGER,
    "Days", INTEGER,
    {
        { "As of", 1, 0 },
        { "1M ago", 2, 30 },
        { "3M ago", 2, 91 },
        { "6M ago", 2, 182 },
        { "1Y ago", 2, 365 },
        { "2Y ago", 2, 730 }
    }
)

// ---- S2 sort and hide
// P6W R Row[Row] ▸ Sort by column ▸ Order (still valid: each Row has one Order). Hide Order and Days.
// R1 ▸ Format ▸ Y axis: nothing to change. If an empty compare bar slot appears, R1 ▸ Y-axis field ▸ "Show items with no
// data" must be OFF (default).

// ---- S3 then: Tabular Editor ▸ run P6A_MEASURES_TE2.csx (build 11a) ▸ Ctrl+S in Power BI.

// ---- S4 check: expect 2 rows, the second labelled with the R1a window ("3M ago" when nothing is picked)
EVALUATE
    SUMMARIZECOLUMNS ( 'P6W R Row'[Row], TREATAS ( { "Hedge fund" }, DIM_COUNTERPARTY[HF Scope] ),
        TREATAS ( { "6M" }, 'P6W R Compare'[Window] ),
        "Face", [P6 R1 Collateral] )
// → "As of" ≈ €63bn and "6M ago" only.
